        <activityName xml:lang="en">Ethanol, 99.7% in H2O, from sugarcane molasses, at distillation</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Ethanol, 99.7% in H2O, from sugarcane molasses, at distillation
The inventory for "ethanol, 99.7% in H2O, from biomass, at distillation, CH" is modelled with ethanol production from sugar cane and molasse from sugar cane in Brazil.;
CAS number: 000064-17-5; 
Formula: C2H6O; 
Synonyms: Alkohol, alcohol dehydrated, algrain, Anhydrol, cologne spirit, cologne spirits (alcohol), Denatured alcohol, Ethyl alcohol, Ethanol, ethanol 200 proof, Ethanol absolute, ethyl hydrate, ethyl hydroxide, fermentation alcohol, grain alcohol,; 
UUID: a728783f-6d59-3c5b-809b-582055bcde5e
Dewatering of ethanol 95% in H2O in Brazil.
Location: The inventory is modelled for Brazil.
Technology: Dewatering of ethanol
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: Total production of ethanol from cane in Brazil  is around 16.6 Mio m3 per a.
Sampling: Literature data. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_a728783f-6d59-3c5b-809b-582055bcde5e.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
